* wiz4up - WizCon4: four-connection packet-mode server with a login on each of
* /wz0-/wz3. Needs: wizi, wizcon (module on the network). Nothing else running on /wz.
* Tear down with wiz4down.
echo * WizCon4 - start 4-connection server with logins on /wz0-/wz3
echo AT+CIPSTA_CUR?>/wz
modem /wz
echo ATE0>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPMODE=0>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPMUX=1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSERVERMAXCONN=4>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSERVER=1,23>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSTO=0>/wz
modem /wz
* (no `modem -t0 /wz` here: -t0 waits FOREVER for the module's next line,
*  which is the first client's 0,CONNECT - swallowed raw before any listener
*  exists, and the client's first keystroke with it. 2026-09-02)
iniz /wz0
iniz /wz1
iniz /wz2
iniz /wz3
xmode /wz0 eko=1
xmode /wz1 eko=1
xmode /wz2 eko=1
xmode /wz3 eko=1
tsmon /wz0&
tsmon /wz1&
tsmon /wz2&
tsmon /wz3&
echo * Up to 4 clients may now connect to port 23.
echo * NOTE: do not read /wz (raw) while connections are active -
echo * raw pops bypass the shared packet parser.
